import LOEIS.A385.A385385.Defs

set_option linter.unusedVariables false

/-!
# A385385

Irregular triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of polyominoes of size k, i.e., connected subsets of k square cells (or vertices), of the n X n flat torus, up to cyclic shifts and reflections of rows and columns, as well as interchange of rows and columns; 1 <= k <= n^2.

The 55 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A385385

/-- Known terms of `flat`, starting at index `1`. -/
def flatData : List flatRetType :=
  [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 4,
    4, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 5, 10, 23,
    44, 80, 87, 86, 49, 32, 10, 5, 1, 1,
